# Tailwind v4 Canonical Classes

Always use the Tailwind CSS v4 canonical form for CSS variable utilities. Never use the legacy `[var(--token)]` syntax.

## Required form

```
bg-(--sofia-primary)
text-(--sofia-primary)
border-(--sofia-primary)
hover:bg-(--sofia-primary-dark)
focus:border-(--sofia-primary)
focus:ring-(--sofia-primary)/15
```

## Forbidden form

```
bg-[var(--sofia-primary)]
text-[var(--sofia-primary)]
border-[var(--sofia-primary)]
hover:bg-[var(--sofia-primary-dark)]
focus:border-[var(--sofia-primary)]
focus:ring-[var(--sofia-primary)]/15
```

## Rule

- When writing or editing Tailwind classes that reference CSS custom properties, always use `utility-(--token)` or `utility-(--token)/opacity`.
- Never write `utility-[var(--token)]`.
- Apply this to all utilities: `bg`, `text`, `border`, `ring`, `fill`, `stroke`, `from`, `to`, `via`, `outline`, `shadow`, etc.
- When touching a file that still uses the old form, convert those classes to the canonical form in the same edit.
